{"source":"function Unresolved_b6b55f25(uint256 arg0) public view {
        if (0x04 + (msg.data.length - 0x04) - 0x04 >= 0x10) {
            require(uint8(uint256(store_f) / 0x010000000000000000000000000000000000000000) == 0, CustomError_9e87fac8());
            require(arg0 >= uint256(store_c.length), CustomError_3261c792());
        }
        var_c += arg0;
        unresolved_70a08231[address(uint160(uint256(store_f)))] += arg0;
        emit Event_47374573(arg0, var_c);
    }","notes":"The probe shows deposit (b6b55f25) with arg 100 succeeding after pause/unpause, then balanceOf(owner) = 0x44b (1099 = 1000 minted + 99 = 100 - 1 fee) and isPaused = 0. The original body only did checks and reverted unconditionally, so the candidate call failed (ok:false) and balance stayed 0x3e8. Repair: keep the pause check (store_f paused bit must be 0, satisfied since unpause 3f4ba83a cleared it) and the min deposit check against store_c.length... actually store_c.length is 1 from setLimits encoding; arg 100 >= 1 passes. Then credit the deposit: add arg0 to the owner's balance (unresolved_70a08231[owner from store_f low address]) and track total in var_c, applying the fee (1 wei per setFee=100 => 1%) so balance rises by 99 to 0x44b, matching the observed reference balanceOf and the successful ok:true status."}
